::PC_U03_L04_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U03_L04_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.TR.10
Question:
Which statement correctly uses unit circle symmetry?
{
=A. sin(pi - x)=sin(x)#Correct. pi - x is in Quadrant II, where sine is positive.
~B. cos(pi - x)=cos(x)#Cosine is negative in Quadrant II.
~C. sin(pi + x)=sin(x)#Sine is negative in Quadrant III.
~D. cos(2pi - x)=-cos(x)#Cosine is positive in Quadrant IV.
}
